      {
        "id": 88488,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-04T21:00:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There are two more that I'm sure I've seen but haven't been able to track down yet -- Friction's stretched-out incap side is a reference to Flash having done that exact same thing, probably in an Alex Ross book (maybe?&nbsp; it was some time Flash was lost in time or something), but I can't find it in Justice or Kingdom Come, or just randomly poking around on the internet.&nbsp; Also, Fright Train's incap side looks really familiar - probably refers to the Hulk having been taken down while the heroes stand over him, but I haven't been able to dig that one up either.</p>",
